    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1156">

                <pb facs="0825" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/111.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul Miller.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-19T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department understands from your telegram of June 15, 8 p.m., that since control
                    of Panuco and Topila districts has passed from General Caballeros to General
                    Aguilar, foreigners in these districts have not been receiving ample protection.
                    It is very essential that ample protection should be given to the lives of
                    foreigners and to every foreign property and enterprise in your district and if
                    it be necessary to insure such protection that troops properly commanded should
                    be immediately distributed through these districts. Navy report made by
                    Lieutenant Shafroth of the <hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi> under date of
                    June 5th indicates that Aguilar will give protection to foreign interests. If
                    ample protection is not being given at this time to foreign oil properties and
                    operators consult Navy officials then telegraph all obtainable details so
                    Department may make energetic protest to Carranza.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
